# Derived and scratch. Nothing here is authored, so nothing here is committed:
# a generated artifact in the index goes stale the moment the source moves, and
# the next reader cannot tell a stale one from a true one. Regenerate instead.
# The one exception, map/parents.jsonl below, carries its own reason: it is
# authored rather than generated, so nothing derives it and it cannot go
# stale against a source the way everything else here does.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Run work packages: journals and response forms, written by the engine.
.agent-work/
# Issue-tier worktrees, one per open root run, beside this checkout.
.worktrees/
# The code map, built by `palette:map` at closeout and read on the spot.
# `.code-map/` is the statement store, `map/` the page tree -- both derived,
# except `map/parents.jsonl`: the map's defined portion, authored by a human
# rather than built, so it is tracked instead of regenerated.
.code-map/
map/*
!map/parents.jsonl
# A coverage run's own tally and pytest's own cache -- both regenerated by
# the next run, so neither is a record of anything the repo needs to keep.
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.claude/worktrees/
